{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_vgd677brrva2kbesgwn5sjy6s67of4kmzgfq4k5dla6qldtez4ia","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. The C library is small (one translation unit) but I verified the *complete* surface rather than assuming.\n\n## Surface enumeration (definition of done)\nBuilt the C library with CMake and ran `nm -D` on `libdriver.so`:\n\n```\nT w_utf8_drop      <- non-static, exported, but NOT in lib.h\nT w_utf8_filter    <- declared in lib.h\n```\nNo namespace/renaming macros in the header, so linker names equal source names.\n\n## Rust exports (`translation/target/release/libdriver.so`)\n```\nT w_utf8_drop\nT w_utf8_filter\n```\n**Symbol diff is empty** — every C export is present, nothing extra leaks.\n\n## Fidelity details preserved\n- **Signed-char comparison** in `valid_2`: `(x)[0] >= (char)0xC2` is a signed compare, reproduced as `(b0 as i8) >= (0xC2u8 as i8)`.\n- **Short-circuit lazy byte reads**: continuation bytes are only read after the preceding mask check passes, so the code never reads past the NUL terminator — same as the C macros.\n- **Redundant/odd conditions kept as-is** (e.g. `(x)[0] != 0xEF || x[1] <= 0xBF` in `valid_3`, which is always true) — no \"fixes\".\n- **Allocator ABI**: calls libc `malloc`/`realloc`/`strdup`/`memcpy`/`strlen` directly, so returned pointers are `free()`-able by the caller exactly as with the C version (`strdup` fast path preserved, including its NULL-on-OOM).\n- **`repl` bookkeeping** reproduced verbatim (grow by 4096 when `repl < 3`, `repl -= 3` per replacement, leaked old pointer on realloc failure → return NULL).\n- **`bool` param** taken as `c_uchar` and tested `!= 0`; confirmed via disassembly that gcc emits `cmpb $0x0`, so any non-zero byte is true — identical ABI without Rust UB on non-canonical values.\n- `assert(string != NULL)` reproduced via glibc `__assert_fail` (same abort path/format; only the embedded source path differs, which is build-dir dependent even in C).\n\n## Differential verification\nBuilt a `dlopen` harness loading both `.so`s side by side and compared `w_utf8_drop` return offsets and `w_utf8_filter` output bytes (plus NULL-ness) for both `replacement` values:\n\n- exhaustive all 1- and 2-byte strings, exhaustive all 3-byte strings for `drop`\n- 4-byte sweep over lead/second bytes × continuation variants (~44M)\n- 400k randomized fuzz strings biased toward UTF-8 boundary bytes\n- long strings (up to 200k bytes) of all-invalid and mixed bytes to exercise the realloc growth path and buffer boundaries\n- hand-picked overlong/surrogate/out-of-range samples\n\n**45,143,491 comparisons, 0 mismatches**, and every returned pointer was `free()`d by the harness without error.\n\nDeliverables: `translation/Cargo.toml` (`crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]`) and `translation/src/lib.rs`; `cargo build --release` compiles warning-free from a clean state. `c_src/` untouched, and my scratch build directory was removed."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":313,"cache_read_input_tokens":45467,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":313,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4aac8de3-9c5b-43be-b369-df9c76b4f9ee","uuid":"2ed1c41f-1ff0-43d8-a343-a384cf29379f","timestamp":"2026-08-27T19:51:30.152Z"}
